Z||000006||Ken Wittlief||08-31-2001||11:47 AM||||I dont want to derail this thread anymore with discussions of DNA and proteins - but I do remember something about proteins all having left handed or right handed molecules, a whole bunch of them in a string, and if even one is the wrong way the protein cannot support life.<P>as for life being made in a test tube - it never happened - they made tar and ammino acids - so how is something going to live in a puddle of tar?! Tar is toxic!<P>Ok - sorry for the sidetrack - back to the dam - there are several flood control dams up here in NY, on the genesse and susquhania rivers - when you see them on 51 weeks of the year you scratch you head and say WTH is this doing here - esp the one north of Letchworth state park on the genesse river - its HUGE! and the river is only about 3 feet deep almost all year.<P> But before the dam was built the remains of a hurricane came through the area and literally came within a hairs breath of wiping out the city of rochester, NY. About 30 miles downstream the Genesse runs right through downtown Rochester.<P>  so now if you go down and see this dam at just the right time in the spring, its full to the top, and its a couple hundred feet high, trapped in a gorge, but the rest of the year it looks like the army corps of engineers got bored and were playing with dumptrucks.<P>  as far as feeling weird by the dam - what is the temp out there in the desert? maybe you are experiencing heat related stress? Maybe they spray some herbicide to keep vegitation from growing around the dam? Maybe thats why they dont want anyone trespessing - there could be toxic chemicals in the area.<P>  I get the impression that several people in this thread are looking for a government conspiricy to get all excited about - it doesnt really matter what it is - simply the excitement of "the government is up to something and I have inside info and I have to figure it out".<P>  the government is not that clever - who invented the airplane? two bicycle mechanics working on there own! who invented the light bulb? a guy who was sent home from public school when he was 11, and his parents were told not to send him back because he is retarded (Edison).<P>  You have to realize the atomic bomb was developed during WW2, and the scientist involved had serious reservations about completing it - the government doesnt invent, develope or reverse engineer things, people do - individual people - engineers and scientist - human beings with parents and wives and children... I beleive that if WW2 was not a factor, the A bomb would never have been invented. It is clear now that if the cold war didnt exist we would still be talking about sending men to the moon for the first time, someday!<P> all the goverenment can do is provide funding and withhold funding, they cant force anyone to do anything that is against their conscience and moral standards.<P>  So it all boils down to this. You either believe in the human race or you dont, you either trust and hope that in the long run humanity will rise up to higher things, accomplish better things, work towards its own ultimate good or you dont. It doenst make any difference what government is in charge or who is controlling the funding.<P>  You want to look for a conspiricy? Make your own conspiricy - figure out something that is important to you, find people with similar intersets, and start doing something with part of your time working towards a long term goal - a positive conspiricy. What you do today determines what your tomorrow will be like.<P> It amazes me that anyone living in this country, with the almost absolute freedom we have, would seriously think the government controls and manipulates us! How could they? you are free to go wherever you want, live wherever you want, work, play, eat... and nobody in the government could care less.<BR> <BR> People come to the US from other countries and send their kids to our public schools, and the kids get straight As and perfect SAT scores, and the parents start their own businesses and make millions of dollars, while we sit around and whine about the government controlling our lives and manipulating our destiny.<P> YIKES!<P>  ||||reg||10
Z||000007||JSocha||08-31-2001||12:32 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR><B>the government doesnt invent, develope or reverse engineer things, people do - individual people - engineers and scientist - human beings with parents and wives and children... I beleive that if WW2 was not a factor, the A bomb would never have been invented.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>You are absolutely 100% correct!<P>But those creative individual people that invent, develope and/or reverse engineer things sometimes are sought out and hired by our (or others respective) Government and some of them do not have a conciousness to spit at and will develope things at the Governments request.  Some good, some not so good, some deadly and/or destructive.<P>For example, how about the Governments future plan and goal to implant microchips within our bodies at birth to track us and that can not be removed later on because of where they want to locate it?  Much like the implants we can have for our pets if they get lost.  Believe it or not, that technology is being further developed by Big Brother right now and as we speak (or write)!<P>Part of the technology they are attempting to implement within these chips is the ability to transmit and subsequently track our location via GPS, our vital signs, information about the individual as time goes on connected into a large database of information about you and a few other things I can not recall at this time.  Our Government.  Not some independent Edison/Einstein of today, but one sought out, retained and working for our Government.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jsocha_2.gif"> ||||reg||7
